domain AgencyRepairPlanning:
  description "Plan the accepted ADR-0027 implementation impact, without runtime changes."

problem P1:
  |
    User requests an implementation impact inventory and repair plan after accepting
    ADR-0027 revision 1. Existing seals record legacy implementation, not completion.

premise P2:
  |
    Preserve ADR-0027 reaction-only psyche and one conscious character, old battle
    generations, engine authority, privacy, no-call and ADR-0025/0026 compatibility.
    The current instruction authorizes investigation and local plan documentation,
    not implementation, paid experiments, deployment or remote writes.

evidence E1:
  |
    Accepted ADR-0027 and the prior acceptance-and-reseal report distinguish
    responsibility acceptance from pending schema, writer, lifetime and generation.
    Current sealgraph contains 22 REF and prior readback had zero stale references.

evidence E2:
  |
    Current types.ts separates CharacterDeepPsycheExpressionStateV2 containing
    currentGoal from CharacterExpressionStateV2 containing emotion, brief and focus.
    openai-compatible.ts generates goals in private phase instructions and already
    returns utterance plus action from advanceCharacterAgent.

evidence E3:
  |
    battle-service.ts builds observer-safe available actions with bound action norms,
    decisionProfile, tacticalNeed and feedback. It has later-bucket action-only
    redecision and accepted-action validation. Compact state acceptance preserves
    previous state; extending provider output alone cannot persist a new goal.

evidence E4:
  |
    Existing plan t026 includes actual-payload fixtures, t027 detailed contracts,
    t028 exact acceptance, t029 implementation, t030-t032 bounded comparison.
    Current branch c63c526 is 20 ahead and zero behind freshly fetched origin/main
    1cdf210; related WIP and graph are retained.

decision I1 based_on E2, E3:
  |
    Most likely repair surfaces are goal/intent ownership, state flow, knowledge
    projection and redecision consistency, not merging two currently separate calls.
    This is an implementation impact inference, not a proven cause of all monotony.

pending U1:
  |
    Concrete field schemas, new generation discriminator, author-goal precedence,
    malformed joint-output handling, full runtime payload fixtures and empirical
    thresholds remain unresolved. No new quality or latency result exists.

premise A1:
  |
    Add goals to the existing expression input alone. This misses the writer,
    acceptance, persistence and later-bucket path and does not satisfy the goal.

premise A2:
  |
    Inventory producers, projections, consumers, state writes and generation paths;
    plan a typed vertical conscious-goal/action/utterance slice plus compatibility
    tests using existing calls where feasible. Defer broad effects and NN work.

decision D1 based_on P1, P2, E1, E2, E3, E4, I1, A1, A2:
  |
    Use A2 to update local impact and repair-plan documents and existing PERT,
    preserving t026 as incomplete until real payload fixtures and rubric are frozen.
    Review source-file evidence, classify mandatory changes versus compatibility
    regression-only surfaces, and map each repair package to acceptance criteria.
    Perform impact before editing sealed plans, then individually reseal reviewed
    changed documents and their affected dependents with previous assertions.

decision D2 based_on P2, E1, U1:
  |
    Keep concrete contract acceptance and paid execution as later gates. Do not
    change accepted ADR text, runtime, prompts, schemas or task completion falsely.
    Declare uninspected paths and missing validation tooling as limitations.
